/-- The kernel accepts the certificate: bounds, separation, properness, and all 1,580 per-vertex
class bindings and separations. -/
theorem deGreyNarrow1420_check : deGreyNarrow1420.check deGrey.verts deGrey.edges = true := by
  first
  | decide +kernel
  | fail "the narrow-fan certificate for pivot 1420 does not check — run #eval (deGreyNarrow1420.firstFault deGrey.verts deGrey.edges).map NarrowFault.report in a scratch file importing Proofs.HadwigerNelson.NarrowFanDiagnose"

/-- **No fan at vertex 1420 of de Grey's graph is narrow**: for every real distance `r`, no
list of vertices avoiding the pivot and all at distance `r` from it is a five-colour fan. The
closing move (`not_colorable_of_spindled_fan`) needs exactly such a fan, so this pivot — one of
the only four in any known graph at the χ ≥ 5 boundary that carry five-colour fans at all —
offers it nothing.

A sceptic re-checks this with: `#print axioms deGrey_no_narrow_fan_1420` (expect exactly
`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`); `scripts/axioms.sh`; and the claims to read aloud —
`Fan` ("every proper colouring paints the pivot like some partner"), `deGrey.point` (the exact
plane embedding at denominator 768), and this statement against the informal one above. -/
theorem deGrey_no_narrow_fan_1420 :
    ∀ (r : ℝ) (Q : List (Fin 1581)), (1420 : Fin 1581) ∉ Q →
      (∀ q ∈ Q, dist (deGrey.point q) (deGrey.point 1420) = r) →
      ¬ Fan (edgeGraph 1581 deGrey.edges) 5 1420 Q :=
  deGreyNarrow1420.sound deGreyNarrow1420_check

end HadwigerNelson
